 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Your neighbor digs a deep basement, and weeks later, your walls crack.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "To dig below the water table, they pump the groundwater out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But that water was helping hold up the soft clay under you.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Without it, the clay slowly squeezes, like a sponge drying out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Your side of the house sinks a little more than the other.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Uneven sinking means cracks, usually over doors and windows.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "That's why builders seal the hole with walls, and watch the houses around it.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Some even pump water back in, to keep the neighbors dry and level.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Now you know. What should we explain next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
